<div class="proj-page-hero">
  <div class="proj-page-label">Project 02 · Jan 2026 – May 2026 · UC San Diego</div>
  <div class="proj-page-title">Orthon — Closed-Loop Sensing and Actuation System for Real-Time Plantar Pressure Offloading</div>
  <div class="proj-page-meta">
    <div class="proj-page-meta-item">Type: <span>Capstone / Team Project</span></div>
    <div class="proj-page-meta-item">Advisor: <span>Dr. Moamen Elhaddad, MD, DPM</span></div>
    <div class="proj-page-meta-item">Team: <span>M2 — 6 members</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="proj-page-tags">
    <span class="tag">Closed-Loop Control</span><span class="tag">Pressure Sensing</span><span class="tag">Nitinol</span><span class="tag">MRF Actuator</span><span class="tag">Custom PCB</span><span class="tag">PI Control</span><span class="tag">Diabetic Foot</span><span class="tag">Embedded Systems</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="proj-content">

  <div class="proj-section">
    <div class="proj-section-title">Overview</div>
    <p>Orthon is a smart insole system that autonomously detects high-pressure plantar regions and actively offloads them in real time to reduce diabetic foot ulcer risk. With over 537 million people living with diabetes globally — projected to reach 643 million by 2030 — and 19–34% developing foot ulcers during their lifetime, pressure offloading is a critical and underserved clinical need.</p>
    <p>The system comprises a layered insole with a pressure sensor array, two actuator module designs (Nitinol lock-ring and Magnetorheological Fluid), a custom PCB, and a closed-loop PI control algorithm that continuously adjusts module height to redistribute plantar load.</p>
    <div class="highlight-box"><p>Clinical targets met: offload pressure by 30–50% · withstand 800–1200 kPa peak plantar pressure · fit within 20 mm height constraint · identify heel strike, midstance, and toe liftoff.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="proj-section">
    <div class="proj-section-title">Key Specifications</div>
    <div class="specs-grid">
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Pressure Offload</div><div class="spec-value">30 – 50%</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Peak Pressure</div><div class="spec-value">800 – 1200 kPa</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Height Constraint</div><div class="spec-value">≤ 20 mm</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Module Stroke</div><div class="spec-value">15 mm → 12 mm</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Control</div><div class="spec-value">Closed-loop PI</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Mapping Algorithm</div><div class="spec-value">IDW (O(h²) error)</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Gait Phases</div><div class="spec-value">Heel strike / Midstance / Toe-off</div></div>
      <div class="spec-cell"><div class="spec-label">Regulatory Target</div><div class="spec-value">Class II device pathway</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="proj-section">
    <div class="proj-section-title">Hardware Design</div>
    <p><strong>Sensing layer:</strong> A pressure sensor array maps plantar pressure distribution in real time. Data is processed via a low-pass moving average filter and mapped using Inverse Distance Weighting (IDW) interpolation with O(h²) accuracy.</p>
    <p><strong>Nitinol Lock-Ring Module:</strong> A flexible nitinol-embedded TPU ring expands when current is applied, releasing the platform from a locked state into a spring-supported offloading position (15 mm → 12 mm drop). This provides passive, energy-efficient offloading.</p>
    <p><strong>MRF (Magnetorheological Fluid) Module:</strong> An electromagnet coil controls the viscosity of MRF through a piston orifice, enabling selective switching between rigid support and soft offloading states. Modules in soft state transfer load to adjacent rigid modules, achieving targeted redistribution.</p>
    <p><strong>Custom PCB:</strong> A bespoke PCB interfaces the sensor array and module controllers, handling power distribution, signal conditioning, and microcontroller communication.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="proj-section">
    <div class="proj-section-title">Control Architecture</div>
    <p>A descending-priority greedy selector algorithm identifies high-pressure spots from the mapped data and assigns offloading priority. A closed-loop PI controller then drives individual module height adjustments to reach target pressure thresholds. Real-time feedback is provided to both the patient (via a display interface) and the clinical team.</p>
    <p>Bench testing confirmed that each excess pressure spike triggers a corresponding rise in module offloading distance, with the actuator dropping to redistribute the localized load — directly validating the offloading strategy.</p>
  </div>

